<h3 style="margin-top:0">Bay groups</h3>
<p class="bm-note">One group per cage, chassis or row of bays, any size (a 5-bay cage is 1 column x 5 rows, or 5 x 1 if the drives stand upright).
Trays are numbered from <i>First tray</i>, counting along rows or down columns, starting at the corner you choose, so the map can match the numbers on your case.
<i>Trays drawn</i>: vertical for drives that stand upright. <i>Placement</i>: put a group next to the one before it (for cages side by side) or below it.
<i>Blank trays</i>: tray numbers that are drawn as a gap (no bay there); they cannot hold a disk.
To place a disk, open it on the Map tab and choose its group and tray.</p>
<div id="bm-box">
<table id="bm-groups">
